-- title:
--   Pole chart of a fibre model localizes at non-affine places
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, and let $fm$ be a `FibreModel` for these data: subrings $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}, B_{\infty}$ of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ N \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, containing the constants from $A$, with $\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N \in B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and $\bar\jmath^{-1} \in B_{\infty}$, each integral over the subring generated by the constants together with $\bar\jmath$, resp. $\bar\jmath^{-1}$, together with ring maps $\pi_{\mathrm{Fin}}, \pi_{\infty}$ into $F_k := \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N = k(j_q, j_{q,N}) \subseteq k((q))$ reducing constants via $\mathrm{red}$ and sending $\bar\jmath \mapsto j_q$, $\bar\jmath_N \mapsto j_{q,N}$. Let $v$ be a place of $F_k$ over $k$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_v \subsetneq F_k$ containing $k$ and whose ring is a principal ideal ring, and assume that $j_q$ and $j_{q,N}$ do not both lie in $\mathcal{O}_v$. Then every $\pi_{\infty}(b)$, $b \in B_{\infty}$, lies in $\mathcal{O}_v$, and every $g \in \mathcal{O}_v$ can be written as $g \cdot \pi_{\infty}(b') = \pi_{\infty}(b)$ with $b, b' \in B_{\infty}$ and $\pi_{\infty}(b')$ not having value $0$ at $v$ (its residue is nonzero, so it is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_v$).
--
--   This is the statement that the reduced pole chart $\pi_{\infty}(B_{\infty})$ of a fibre model of $X_0(N)$ at a prime $\ell \nmid N$ is centred at every place of the fibre function field at which $j_q$ and $j_{q,N}$ are not both regular — the non-affine places, the cusps — and localizes there to the full valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$. It is used in the construction of charts and coordinates around such places, in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_isChartAt_of_not_isAffineGeomPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_isChartAt_of_not_isAffineGeomPlace), [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.hasCoordinates_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.hasCoordinates_of_sp_eq_spPlace) and the cusp law at infinity for prolongation tuples; the proof cites the surjectivity of $\mathrm{red}$ and the separability of $j_{q,N}$ over $k(j_q)$ when $\ell \nmid N$.
-- source:
